ot_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nAfter DEC-0001 selects the framework, package manager, and CI baseline, create\nthe smallest reproducible project skeleton for the shared game core, web\nadapter, and PWA adapter. Document one bootstrap, format, lint, and\ndeterministic test command interface, and make a clean approved-runtime\ncheckout run a deterministic sample test. This task establishes boundaries and\ntooling only; it does not implement game behaviour or resolve the decision.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThis is the first implementation contract and has no R-series dependencies.\nGATE-0001 / DEC-0001 is retained as a human implementation precondition:\nauthoring this runbook does not select a stack, and implementation must stop\nbefore selecting or installing framework, package-manager, or CI tooling.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- Root build and tooling configuration, including the pinned toolchain\n  declaration and command mapping.\n- `src/core/`, `src/content/`, `src/app/`, `src/platform/web/`, and\n  `src/platform/pwa/` ownership directories, created without feature code.\n- `tests/` and an isolated deterministic sample-test location.\n- `docs/development.md`, which records the approved-runtime bootstrap,\n  format, lint, and deterministic-test commands once DEC-0001 is decided.\n- The build/test command interface: `bootstrap`, `format`, `lint`, and\n  `test:deterministic` (or the selected tool's documented equivalent).\n\n## Behaviour\n\nUse the DEC-0001-approved runtime only. Pin its version and package-manager\nlock/metadata as appropriate to that approved selection. Create the isolated\ndirectory skeleton so later work has distinct shared-core, content, app,\nweb-adapter, PWA-adapter, and test ownership.\n\nConfigure the selected tooling so the documented command interface has a\nsingle reproducible mapping for bootstrap, formatting, linting, and a\ndeterministic sample test. The sample test must use no wall clock, network,\nplayer data, browser storage, renderer, or platform feature. Record the exact\ncommands and a clean-checkout result in `docs/development.md`.\n\nThe skeleton must preserve the canonical direction: target adapters are\nseparate from the shared deterministic core, and no directory implies that a\ntarget may change campaign rules. Later R0002 owns enforcement of detailed\ncore/adapter dependency rules.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nThe responsive web and installable PWA targets receive separate adapter\ndirectories only. Neither adapter gains a renderer, service worker, cache\nlifecycle, browser API dependency, or target-specific campaign behaviour in\nthis task. PWA installation, caching, offline delivery, and update activation\nremain later scoped work; the PWA directory is an ownership boundary, not an\nimplementation of those features.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not resolve DEC-0001 or choose a framework, package manager, CI provider,\nhost, storage API, browser/device matrix, or performance budget. Do not add\ngameplay, campaign state, content, UI screens, renderer code, input handling,\nservice worker, persistence, network client, accounts, diagnostics, hosting,\nor release automation. Do not claim browser/PWA compatibility or release\nreadiness.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. The baseline contains only source,\nconfiguration, test, and developer-documentation boundaries. Do not create or\nadd incidental product visuals, UI assets, illustrations, icons, fonts,\ntextures, sprites, maps, audio-visual assets, or copied reference styling;\n`asset_ids` remains blank.\n\n## Audio assessment\n\n`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`. Do not create, add, reserve, or reference\nmusic, sound effects, voice, or other product audio; the blank audio metadata\nand zero duration intentionally record that exclusion.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Before implementation, confirm DEC-0001 is accepted and record the approved\n  runtime, package manager, CI baseline, and pinned versions. If it remains\n  unresolved, stop implementation and report GATE-0001 without substituting a\n  tool choice.\n- In a clean checkout of the approved runtime, run the exact documented\n  bootstrap command, format check, lint check, and deterministic sample-test\n  command.\n- Verify the documented ownership directories exist and that the sample test\n  is isolated from browser, network, storage, clock, and product data.\n- Preserve command output, pinned-toolchain evidence, directory listing, and\n  the deterministic test result in the implementation evidence.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`docs/development.md` must identify the selected command mapping and pinned\ntoolchain only after DEC-0001. The implementation record must retain the clean\ncheckout command outputs and show the isolated ownership directories. If the\ngate is still blocked, retain this runbook and record that no implementation\ntooling or product work was created.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- An approved-runtime clean checkout can run the documented bootstrap, format,\n  lint, and deterministic sample-test commands successfully.\n- Shared core, content, app, web-adapter, PWA-adapter, and test ownership\n  directories are isolated without feature, renderer, storage, or service\n  implementation.\n- GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 remains explicit; this task neither selects the stack\n  nor claims implementation, browser, PWA, or release readiness before that\n  decision.\n- No product visual or audio asset is created or introduced.\n{\n  \"manifest_id\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4-runbook-authoring-ledger\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"purpose\": \"Persistent, append-only allocation ledger for bounded B-series authoring batches and immutable R-series implementation contracts. It allocates the current catalogue only; queued shards remain expansion work.\",\n  \"project_slug\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4\",\n  \"source_catalogue\": \"planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\n  \"expected_runbook_count\": 12,\n  \"id_counters\": {\"next_authoring_batch_id\": \"B0007\", \"next_implementation_runbook_id\": \"R0013\", \"rule\": \"Never reuse, renumber, or replace an accepted B or R ID. Append new allocations using these counters only.\"},\n  \"wave\": {\"number\": 1, \"state\": \"planned\", \"checkpoint_after_each_batch\": true, \"resume_from\": \"first batch whose state is not accepted; validate accepted IDs, paths, and provenance before dispatch\", \"recovery\": \"If a batch fails, retain its IDs, mark it blocked or repairable, repair only its listed output paths, validate its contracts, then resume that same batch. Do not reallocate its R IDs.\"},\n  \"dispatch_history\": [\n    {\"dispatcher\":\"D0001\",\"sequence\":8,\"state\":\"complete\",\"expanded_chapter\":null,\"new_imp_contract_ids\":[],\"new_authoring_batches\":[],\"ready_unassigned_contract_ids\":[],\"queued_chapters_remaining\":[\"SHARD-02\",\"SHARD-03\",\"SHARD-04\"],\"held_chapters_remaining\":[\"SHARD-05\"],\"blocking_gates\":{\"SHARD-02\":[\"GATE-0004\"],\"SHARD-03\":[\"GATE-0002\",\"GATE-0003\",\"GATE-0004\"],\"SHARD-04\":[\"GATE-0002\",\"GATE-0005\",\"GATE-0007\"],\"SHARD-05\":[\"GATE-0006\"]},\"successor_dispatcher\":\"D0002\",\"checkpoint\":\"Validated catalogue/manifest unique IMP, B, and R IDs; all 12 catalogue contracts are allocated exactly once; SHARD-02 is the first queued chapter but remains ineligible while DEC-0004/GATE-0004 is unresolved. No contract allocation, counter advance, or accepted work overwrite occurred.\"}\n  ],\n  \"catalogue_disposition\": {\"allocated\": [\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0008\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0010\",\"IMP-0011\",\"IMP-0012\"], \"deferred\": [], \"human_gates_retained\": {\"IMP-0001\":\"GATE-0001\", \"IMP-0006\":\"GATE-0003\", \"IMP-0007\":\"GATE-0003\", \"IMP-0009\":\"GATE-0005\", \"IMP-0010\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004\"}},\n  \"queued_expansion\": [\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-02\",\"title\":\"Campaign content and domain logic\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 2 after GATE-0004\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand into bounded IMP records before assigning any R IDs\"},\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-03\",\"title\":\"Session, UI, input, and accessibility\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 3 after GATE-0002,GATE-0003,GATE-0004\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand after its predecessor shards; preserve shared UI and web-adapter ownership\"},\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-04\",\"title\":\"PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\",\"SHARD-03\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 4 after GATE-0002,GATE-0005,GATE-0007\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand only after the session/UI and campaign contracts exist\"},\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-05\",\"title\":\"Connected-scope decision package\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"state\":\"hold\",\"future_wave\":\"only if explicitly authorised after GATE-0006\",\"allocation_rule\":\"no P0 implementation R contracts\"}\n  ],\n  \"context_packet_baseline\": {\n    \"terminology\": [\"B-series = authoring runbook\", \"R-series = generated implementation runbook\", \"IMP-series = catalogue contract\", \"shared core\", \"web adapter\", \"PWA delivery adapter\", \"local save\", \"cache\", \"human gate\"],\n    \"target_constraints\": [\"original offline-capable 2D single-player RPG\", \"responsive web and installable PWA\", \"keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad\", \"no accounts, sync, multiplayer, purchases, or network services in P0\", \"shared core must not import platform/render/network modules\", \"PWA cache and save data remain separate\"],\n    \"required_templates\": [\"runbooks/TEMPLATE.md\", \"runbooks/F014.md provenance and asset-assessment requirements\"],\n    \"authoring_rules\": [\"write only assigned paths\", \"preserve gates and unanswered questions\", \"do not create incidental assets when asset_impact is not_applicable\", \"perform structural, not product-release, validation\"]\n  },\n  \"batches\": [\n    {\"id\":\"B0001\",\"order\":1,\"title\":\"Bootstrap decision-gated foundation\",\"state\":\"accepted\",\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 is retained inside R0001 and blocks implementation only\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0001\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/platform-appendix.md\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0001\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validated R0001 metadata, provenance, output ownership, explicit GATE-0001 disposition, and baseline-command evidence; batch checkpoint complete\",\"recovery\":\"keep R0001 reserved; author it before, not after, the gate\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"one bounded R runbook\",\"gate is explicit\",\"baseline command and ownership evidence are specified\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0002\",\"order\":2,\"title\":\"Shared seams, deterministic harness, and token contract\",\"state\":\"accepted\",\"depends_on_batches\":[],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0001 is an implementation dependency only; R0010 retains GATE-0002,GATE-0004\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0010\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0010\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validated R0002/R0003/R0010 metadata, provenance, dependencies, ownership, required sections, and retained gates against the manifest\",\"recovery\":\"repair only R0002,R0003,R0010; never split or renumber accepted contracts\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"core/adapter seam precedes feature work\",\"fixture and token outputs have distinct ownership\",\"all gates retained\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0003\",\"order\":3,\"title\":\"Deterministic state slice and connected-scope exclusion\",\"state\":\"accepted\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0002\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0002 accepted\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0004\",\"R0008\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0008\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validated R0004/R0008 metadata, provenance, dependencies, ownership, and required sections against the manifest\",\"recovery\":\"retain IDs and repair the failed R contract only\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"vertical foundation slice remains independently reviewable\",\"P0 connected-service exclusion is explicit\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0004\",\"order\":4,\"title\":\"Content validation and local recovery protocols\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0003\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0003 accepted; R0006 requires GATE-0003\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0005\",\"R0006\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate content/save boundaries and retained storage gate\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0005,R0006 and rerun the blocked item after its decision\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"content and save/cache ownership is separated\",\"save recovery remains a bounded foundation slice\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0005\",\"order\":5,\"title\":\"Migration, diagnostics, and provenance controls\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0004\"],\"parallel_with\":[\"B0006 after B0004 acceptance, except R0007 still waits for R0006\"],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0007 needs GATE-0003; R0009 needs GATE-0005\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0007\",\"R0009\",\"R0011\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\",\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0011\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate migration, diagnostics, and provenance fields; record unresolved gates\",\"recovery\":\"rerun only incomplete assigned IDs; preserve any accepted R contract\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"no transport or remote diagnostics is introduced\",\"provenance review is explicit\",\"contracts remain at most three\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0006\",\"order\":6,\"title\":\"Foundation documentation closure\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0004\",\"B0003\"],\"parallel_with\":[\"B0005 after B0004 acceptance\"],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0006 must be accepted or documented as blocked; no gate is implicitly resolved\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0012\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0012\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"cross-check all foundation ownership, dependencies, and gates before accepting the wave\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0012 and correct only its documentation contract\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"documentation concludes the foundation slice without claiming implementation or approval\",\"gated save work remains visible\"]}\n  ],\n  \"r_contracts\": [\n    {\"id\":\"R0001\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0001\",\"title\":\"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\",\"dependencies\":[],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0001\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0001\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No product asset work; establish only project/tooling boundaries and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"documented deterministic baseline command\",\"isolated ownership directories\",\"GATE-0001 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and path; repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0002\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0002\",\"title\":\"Enforce shared-core and adapter dependency seams\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0002.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#dependency-direction-and-state-rules\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0002\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; this is an interface and dependency-policy contract.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"forbidden core imports rejected\",\"adapter command-only fixture\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0003\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0003\",\"title\":\"Create deterministic test and fixture harness\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0003.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#observability-quality-evidence-and-release-verification\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0003\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; fixtures use non-product deterministic data.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"repeatable fixture result\",\"isolated fixture storage\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0004\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0004\",\"title\":\"Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0004\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0003\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; state envelopes deliberately exclude authored content.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"stale and invalid commands do not mutate state\",\"duplicate interaction is idempotent\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0005\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0003\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0005\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0004\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No art/audio assets; reserve only schema/provenance fields for later original assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"valid minimal package passes\",\"invalid references fail\",\"reachability fixture\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0006\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0006\",\"title\":\"Specify local save and recovery protocol\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0006\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0004\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; protocol is data/recovery only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"fault fixtures cover write and validation failures\",\"save/cache separation\",\"GATE-0003 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID; wait for storage decision before accepting gated work\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0007\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0007\",\"title\":\"Define pure save migration runner\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\",\"R0006\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0007\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; migration fixtures retain original bytes only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"predecessors migrate once\",\"failed candidate remains intact\",\"GATE-0003 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and resume after R0006/gate closure\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0008\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0008\",\"title\":\"Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0008\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0003\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; a negative scope boundary.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"no identity/token/network fields\",\"future connected work remains gated\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0009\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0009\",\"title\":\"Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0006\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0009\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; local redacted records only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"consent and deletion controls\",\"payload redaction\",\"no network transport\",\"GATE-0005 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and wait for privacy gate where required\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0010\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0010\",\"title\":\"Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0010\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No final artwork, fonts, or icons; semantic tokens only and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"non-colour cues\",\"reduced motion values\",\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and await numeric design decisions\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0011\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0011\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets are created; this contract defines provenance controls for later asset-required work.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"missing provenance rejected\",\"human creative review recorded\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0012\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\",\"R0006\",\"R0008\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0012\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0006\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"all foundation ownership/dependencies/gates cross-checked\",\"does not claim release readiness\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this documentation contract\"}\n  ]\n}\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Structural quality gate for generated B-series and R-series runbooks.\n\nThis validates planning artefacts only; it is never product or release evidence.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nREPOSITORY = ROOT.parents[1]\nMANIFEST_PATH = ROOT / \"planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"\nCATALOGUE_PATH = ROOT / \"planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\"\nR_ID, F_ID = re.compile(r\"^R\\d{4}$\"), re.compile(r\"^F\\d{3}$\")\n\ndef values(value):\n    return value if isinstance(value, list) else ([value] if value else [])\n\ndef parse_value(value):\n    value = value.strip().strip(\"\\\"'\")\n    if value == \"[]\": return []\n    if value.startswith(\"[\") and value.endswith(\"]\"):\n        return [item.strip().strip(\"\\\"'\") for item in value[1:-1].split(\",\") if item.strip()]\n    return value\n\ndef front_matter(path):\n    text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    if not text.startswith(\"---\\n\"): return {}\n    end = text.find(\"\\n---\", 4)\n    if end < 0: return {}\n    result, key = {}, None\n    for line in text[4:end].splitlines():\n        if line.lstrip().startswith(\"-\") and key:\n            result.setdefault(key, []).append(parse_value(line.split(\"-\", 1)[1]))\n        elif \":\" in line:\n            key, value = line.split(\":\", 1); key = key.strip(); result[key] = parse_value(value)\n    return result\n\ndef headings(path):\n    return {re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"-\", match.group(1).lower()).strip(\"-\")\n            for match in re.finditer(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+?)\\s*$\", path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"), re.M)}\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--wave\", help=\"validate allocations through this B batch\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    manifest = json.loads(MANIFEST_PATH.read_text())\n    catalogue = json.loads(CATALOGUE_PATH.read_text())\n    batches = {b[\"id\"]: b for b in manifest[\"batches\"]}\n    contracts = manifest[\"r_contracts\"]\n    if args.wave:\n        if args.wave not in batches: parser.error(\"unknown B batch: \" + args.wave)\n        contracts = [c for c in contracts if batches.get(c.get(\"authoring_batch\"), {}).get(\"order\", 999) <= batches[args.wave][\"order\"]]\n    records = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in catalogue[\"contracts\"]}\n    errors, missing, blocked, unverified = [], [], [], []\n    def fail(text): errors.append(text)\n    ids = [c.get(\"id\", \"\") for c in contracts]\n    if ids != sorted(ids): fail(\"manifest R IDs are not sequence ordered\")\n    for item, count in Counter(ids).items():\n        if count > 1: fail(\"duplicate manifest R ID \" + item)\n    paths = [c.get(\"output_path\", \"\") for c in contracts]\n    for item, count in Counter(paths).items():\n        if count > 1: fail(\"duplicate output path \" + item)\n    assets, browser_paths = {}, defaultdict(list)\n    # The authoring collection is part of the gate: each allocated batch must\n    # exist, identify itself, and be the sole owner of its manifest R IDs.\n    for batch_id, batch_record in batches.items():\n        batch_path = ROOT / \"authoring-runbooks\" / f\"{batch_id}.md\"\n        meta = front_matter(batch_path) if batch_path.is_file() else {}\n        if not meta: fail(f\"{batch_id}: missing or invalid B-series front matter\")\n        elif meta.get(\"task_id\") != batch_id: fail(f\"{batch_id}: task ID mismatch in authoring runbook\")\n        if len(batch_record.get(\"r_contract_ids\", [])) > 7: fail(f\"{batch_id}: exceeds seven-contract batch limit\")\n    for contract in contracts:\n        rid, batch = contract.get(\"id\", \"\"), contract.get(\"authoring_batch\", \"\")\n        if not R_ID.fullmatch(rid): fail(f\"invalid R ID {rid!r}\")\n        if batch not in batches or rid not in batches.get(batch, {}).get(\"r_contract_ids\", []): fail(f\"{rid}: authoring batch ownership mismatch\")\n        catalogue_ids = values(contract.get(\"source_catalogue_ids\"))\n        if not catalogue_ids or contract.get(\"catalogue_id\") not in catalogue_ids: fail(f\"{rid}: missing or inconsistent catalogue provenance\")\n        for cid in catalogue_ids:\n            if cid not in records: fail(f\"{rid}: unknown catalogue ID {cid}\")\n        if contract.get(\"catalogue_id\") in records and not records[contract[\"catalogue_id\"]].get(\"requirement_ids\"): fail(f\"{rid}: catalogue record lacks requirement links\")\n        specs = values(contract.get(\"source_specifications\"))\n        if not specs: fail(f\"{rid}: missing source_specifications\")\n        for link in specs:\n            file_name, _, anchor = link.partition(\"#\"); source = ROOT / file_name\n            if not link.startswith(\"specification/\") or not source.is_file() or (anchor and anchor not in headings(source)):\n                fail(f\"{rid}: unresolved canonical specification link {link}\")\n        stages = values(contract.get(\"factory_stages\"))\n        if not stages or any(not F_ID.fullmatch(s) for s in stages): fail(f\"{rid}: invalid factory_stages\")\n        for dependency in values(contract.get(\"dependencies\")):\n            if dependency not in ids: fail(f\"{rid}: dependency {dependency} is outside allocation\")\n            elif dependency >= rid: fail(f\"{rid}: dependency {dependency} does not precede contract\")\n        impact, asset_ids = contract.get(\"asset_impact\"), values(contract.get(\"asset_ids\"))\n        if impact not in {\"required\", \"not_applicable\"}: fail(f\"{rid}: invalid asset_impact\")\n        if \"asset_ids\" not in contract: fail(f\"{rid}: asset_ids absent\")\n        if impact == \"required\":\n            if not asset_ids or not contract.get(\"asset_brief\") or not contract.get(\"visual_style_version\"): fail(f\"{rid}: required assets lack IDs, brief, or style version\")\n            for asset in asset_ids:\n                if not re.fullmatch(r\"ASSET-[A-Z0-9-]+\", asset): fail(f\"{rid}: unstable asset ID {asset}\")\n                if asset in assets: fail(f\"asset {asset} ambiguously owned by {assets[asset]} and {rid}\")\n                assets[asset] = rid\n        elif asset_ids: fail(f\"{rid}: non-asset contract reserves asset IDs\")\n        if batches.get(batch, {}).get(\"state\") in {\"blocked_on_gate\", \"blocked\", \"repairable\"}: blocked.append(rid)\n        r_path = REPOSITORY / contract.get(\"output_path\", \"\")\n        if not r_path.is_file(): missing.append(rid); continue\n        meta = front_matter(r_path)\n        for field in (\"task_id\", \"sequence\", \"source_specifications\", \"source_catalogue_ids\", \"authoring_batch\", \"factory_stages\", \"asset_impact\", \"asset_ids\"):\n            if field not in meta: fail(f\"{rid}: {r_path.name} lacks {field}\")\n        if \"requirement_ids\" not in meta: fail(f\"{rid}: {r_path.name} lacks requirement_ids\")\n        if meta.get(\"task_id\") != rid: fail(f\"{rid}: task ID mismatch\")\n        if values(meta.get(\"requirement_ids\")) != records.get(contract.get(\"catalogue_id\"), {}).get(\"requirement_ids\", []): fail(f\"{rid}: requirement_ids differ from catalogue\")\n        for field in (\"source_specifications\", \"source_catalogue_ids\", \"authoring_batch\", \"factory_stages\", \"asset_impact\", \"asset_ids\"):\n            if values(meta.get(field)) != values(contract.get(field)): fail(f\"{rid}: {field} differs from manifest\")\n        browser, specs = meta.get(\"browser_impact\", \"not_applicable\"), values(meta.get(\"playwright_spec\", meta.get(\"playwright_specs\")))\n        if browser == \"not_applicable\" and specs: fail(f\"{rid}: browser path on non-browser contract\")\n        if browser != \"not_applicable\" and (not specs or not set(records.get(contract.get(\"catalogue_id\"), {}).get(\"targets\", [])) & {\"web\", \"pwa\"}): fail(f\"{rid}: browser metadata outside browser behaviour scope\")\n        for spec in specs: browser_paths[spec].append(rid)\n        body = r_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        if \"## Verification\" not in body: unverified.append(rid)\n        if not re.search(r\"^## Asset assessment\\s*$\", body, re.M | re.I): fail(f\"{rid}: missing explicit Asset assessment section\")\n    for path, owners in browser_paths.items():\n        if len(owners) > 1: fail(f\"duplicate browser test path {path}: {', '.join(owners)}\")\n    graph = {c[\"id\"]: values(c.get(\"dependencies\")) for c in contracts}; active, done = set(), set()\n    def visit(node):\n        if node in active: fail(\"unsupported circular dependency through \" + node); return\n        if node not in done:\n            active.add(node)\n            for dep in graph[node]:\n                if dep in graph: visit(dep)\n            active.remove(node); done.add(node)\n    for node in graph: visit(node)\n    # Discovered families need a canonical source and a category-appropriate\n    # catalogue/verification route. Explicitly held connected scope is a valid\n    # reviewed outcome, not a missing P0 implementation contract.\n    review = ROOT / \"specification/domain-completeness-review.md\"\n    for line in review.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n        if not line.startswith(\"|\") or line.startswith(\"| System\") or line.startswith(\"| ---\"): continue\n        cells = [cell.strip() for cell in line.split(\"|\")[1:-1]]\n        if len(cells) != 5: continue\n        family, source, _deps, authoring, decision = cells\n        if \"SPEC-\" not in source: fail(f\"domain family {family}: no specification chapter\")\n        if \"hold\" in decision.lower(): continue\n        keywords = [word.lower() for word in re.findall(r\"[A-Za-z]{5,}\", family)]\n        searchable = json.dumps(catalogue).lower()\n        if not any(word in searchable for word in keywords): fail(f\"domain family {family}: no catalogue traceability\")\n        if authoring.lower() not in {\"none\", \"n/a\"} and not authoring: fail(f\"domain family {family}: no content/authoring approach\")\n    allocated = {c.get(\"catalogue_id\") for c in contracts}\n    unallocated = [cid for cid in records if cid not in allocated]\n    print(\"Runbook-generation structural quality gate (not product/release evidence)\")\n    chapter_count = len(list((ROOT / \"specification\").glob(\"*.md\")))\n    source_link_count = sum(len(values(c.get(\"source_specifications\"))) for c in contracts)\n    print(f\"canonical specification chapters: {chapter_count}\")\n    print(f\"specification provenance links: {source_link_count}\")\n    for label, result in ((\"catalogue contracts\", list(records)), (\"manifest contracts\", ids), (\"R files missing\", missing), (\"blocked contracts\", blocked), (\"unverified contracts\", unverified), (\"unallocated catalogue contracts\", unallocated), (\"reserved asset IDs\", list(assets)), (\"browser test paths\", list(browser_paths))):\n        print(f\"{label}: {len(result)}\" + (\" (\" + \", \".join(sorted(result)) + \")\" if result else \"\"))\n    for error in errors: print(\"ERROR:\", error)\n    return 1 if errors or missing or unverified else 0\nif __name__ == \"__main__\": sys.exit(main())\n# Product brief \u2014 Mock Fantasy Quest 4\n\n**Source of truth:** [`INITIAL.md`](INITIAL.md). This normalized brief supports\ndownstream planning; it preserves source scope and records unknowns rather than\nchoosing them.\n\n## Product problem and outcome\n\nCasual adult players need a compact, approachable fantasy RPG that delivers a\ncomplete story without requiring a long commitment or dependable connection.\nThe first useful session is successful when a new player finishes a first\nturn-based battle and understands how to save and resume. The release outcome\nis an original short campaign that a player can complete through exploration,\ndialogue, quests, combat, rewards, saving, and a short ending.\n\n## Category, users, and core experience\n\n| Area | Normalized first-release statement |\n| --- | --- |\n| Category | Deliberately small, offline-capable, 2D single-player fantasy RPG. |\n| Users | Casual and adult players, including people using keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad, captions, adjustable text, and visual settings. |\n| Campaign boundary | One town, one dungeon, and one guided, short ending; no further regions or chapters are required. |\n| Core loop | Explore, converse, accept or advance a quest, enter party-based turn-based combat, manage rewards/inventory, save, and continue. |\n| Experience direction | Original warm hand-painted fantasy, readable silhouettes, and a restrained palette. |\n| Functional reference | *Final Fantasy V* may inform only the high-level scope of a party-based turn-based adventure. |\n\n## Selected target systems\n\n| Target | First-release role | Input model | Delivery constraints | Out-of-scope boundary |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Responsive public web application | Primary browser surface for the complete game. | Keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad. | Responsive phone/tablet/desktop layout; browser compatibility and performance budget must be approved before implementation. | Native binaries, a separate web-only campaign, and browser-exclusive mechanics. |\n| Progressive web app (PWA) | Installable delivery of the same shared game core. | Same inputs where the browser/device supports them. | Offline assets and save-data behavior; safe update/cache refresh must preserve confirmed player data. | A PWA-exclusive campaign, mandatory continuous connection, or a different ruleset. |\n\nThe product uses a shared core with platform adaptation only where necessary.\nIt should work on widely used devices and under feasible slow-network\nconditions; exact supported browsers, device classes, storage quotas, and\nnetwork floor are open decisions.\n\n## First-release scope and measurable success measures\n\nIncluded scope: playable exploration; one town and one dungeon; narrative,\ndialogue, quests, progression and a short ending; onboarding/tutorial; at least\none tutorialized turn-based battle; inventory and rewards; save/load, resume,\ncheckpoints, data-loss recovery; settings and accessibility; audio/visual\nfeedback; content/level delivery; and crash reporting with player-facing error\nrecovery. The source also names account/identity, multiplayer/player safety,\nlive-service operations, and purchase/entitlement handling, but their release\nstatus remains contingent on the explicit conflict decision below.\n\nThe release is measurable when:\n\n- A new player can finish the tutorial battle, create a save, reload it, and\n  reach the short ending on each supported target.\n- The delivered campaign contains exactly one town, one dungeon, and one short\n  ending; added regions or chapters are not needed for release completion.\n- Both targets meet their stated input role; the PWA is installable and each\n  target has a tested offline, save, update, and error-recovery path.\n- Dialogue, inventory, quest, and progression UI are readable with approved\n  accessibility settings, and captions/visual settings are available where the\n  corresponding feedback exists.\n- An interruption, recoverable error, or safe update offers a player-facing\n  recovery path and does not silently discard the last confirmed save.\n\n## Later roadmap, non-goals, and reference boundary\n\nDeferred roadmap: live events/seasonal content, player-created/shared content\n(levels, mods, designs, stories), advanced analytics, and advanced\nmonetisation. They are excluded from first-release acceptance.\n\nNon-goals: copied branding, assets, text, layouts, characters, story/lore,\naudio, maps, or distinctive interactions; additional towns/dungeons/campaigns;\nnative apps; and platform-specific game variants. No cloud-sync, payment,\nmoderation, service-uptime, or backend commitment is implied before approval.\n\n| Reference boundary | Prohibited | Permitted |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Branding and copy | Names, logos, trademarks, marketing copy, story text, dialogue, characters, and world/lore. | A high-level description of a compact party-based turn-based adventure. |\n| Assets and presentation | Art, music, sound, maps, screen composition, visual language, and layouts. | Original art and UI that fulfil this brief\u2019s own direction. |\n| Interaction design | Reproducing distinctive combat screens, menus, flows, quests, or interaction choreography. | Independently designed mechanics and feedback appropriate to the requested scope. |\n\n## Constraints and safe assumptions\n\nExplicit constraints: web/PWA delivery, offline play, accessibility,\nlocalisation, privacy, safe save/recovery, slow-network feasibility, and\noriginal expression. Safe working assumptions: the offline core does not block\non a remote service; content/UI are original; local persistence is durable\nenough for confirmed saves where browser storage permits; connected features,\nif approved, degrade visibly; and crash diagnostics minimize personal data.\nThese are guardrails, not approval of a stack, vendor, backend, account model,\ndata-retention policy, or technical promise.\n\n## Open decisions requiring human approval\n\n1. **Offline versus connected scope:** Reconcile the offline single-player\n   premise with required account identity, multiplayer safety, live operations,\n   and purchase/entitlement handling. Classify each as release-critical,\n   optional connected enhancement, or deferred.\n2. **Account and data policy:** Decide whether accounts are absent, optional,\n   or mandatory; then define authentication, sync/conflict behavior, retention,\n   deletion, and offline/service-outage recovery.\n3. **Multiplayer, commerce, and safety:** State whether multiplayer or\n   real-money purchases actually ship, plus age rating, regions, moderation,\n   reporting, refunds, store, and applicable legal obligations.\n4. **Technical delivery baseline:** Choose engine/framework, repository and CI\n   constraints, browser/device matrix, performance budget, offline-storage\n   quota, update activation policy, error-reporting provider, and cost model.\n5. **Production content and access:** Approve party size, encounter/quest\n   counts, combat/progression balance, language set, audio scope, and the exact\n   accessibility options before production planning.\n# Canonical specification index\n\nThis directory is the canonical, resumable specification for **mock-fantasy-quest-4**. It consolidates F001\u2013F010 without overriding [`INITIAL.md`](../INITIAL.md), which remains the source of truth. A later author must cite stable IDs here rather than rediscovering scope.\n\n## Control rules\n\n- **P0** is an original, offline-capable 2D single-player fantasy RPG: one town, one dungeon, a short guided campaign and ending, exploration, dialogue/quests, party turn combat, inventory, local saves/recovery, settings/accessibility, responsive web, and PWA distribution.\n- Target-neutral rules live in `requirements.*`; the web/PWA differences live in `platform-appendix.md`. PWA is a delivery adaptation of the shared game, not a second game.\n- `Final Fantasy V` is a functional scope reference for party-based turn adventure only. It permits no copied expression: names, lore, text, art, music, maps, layouts, UI flows, or interaction choreography.\n- `proposed` requirements and every `GATE-*` are not implementation authorisation. Resolve their linked `DEC-*` record before allocating dependent work.\n\n## Chapter register\n\n| Chapter ID | Document / owner | Depends on | State |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| SPEC-00 | `00-domain-discovery.md` / product discovery | INITIAL | complete |\n| SPEC-01 | `01-product-brief.md` / product | SPEC-00 | complete |\n| SPEC-02 | `02-feature-model.md` / game design | SPEC-00\u201301 | complete |\n| SPEC-03 | `03-technical-contract.md` / technical design | SPEC-00\u201302 | complete |\n| SPEC-04 | `04-experience-contract.md` / experience design | SPEC-00\u201303 | complete |\n| SPEC-11 | `requirements.md`, `requirements.json` / F011 specification owner | SPEC-00\u201304, planning 05\u201310 | complete |\n| SPEC-12 | `traceability-matrix.md` / F011 specification owner | SPEC-11 | complete; runbook IDs pending F012+ |\n| SPEC-13 | `decision-log.md` / product owner | SPEC-00\u201304 | open decisions recorded |\n| SPEC-14 | `platform-appendix.md` / technical + experience owner | SPEC-11 | complete; thresholds gated |\n| SPEC-15 | `domain-completeness-review.md` / F011 specification owner | SPEC-00\u201304, SPEC-11 | complete; gated domains retained |\n\n## Bounded expansion protocol\n\nExpand one domain chapter at a time, preserving IDs and this register: identify entities/rules, authoring inputs, dependencies, P0 boundary, target adaptations, verification, and open decisions. Proposed detailed chapters are shell/session, campaign content, combat, progression/inventory, persistence/recovery, experience/accessibility, PWA/release, and connected-scope holds. A chapter can move from `planned` to `complete` only when its requirements, trace rows, and decision/risk links exist; it never closes a human gate.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -C 3 'Invalid runbook metadata line|metadata line|front.?matter|runbook metadata' supervisor scripts projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4 --glob '*.py' --glob '*.md'; sed -n '1,220p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/TEMPLATE.md 2>/dev/null; sed -n '1,220p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/F014.md 2>/dev/null; rg -n -C 2 'B0001|R0001|IMP-0001' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md-30-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md-31-## Required authoring content\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md-32-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md:33:For each output, use standard Supervisor front matter and the exact manifest\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md-34-provenance (`source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md-35-B0002`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`) plus `asset_impact:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md-36-not_applicable` and blank `asset_ids`, plus `audio_impact: not_applicable`,\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md-25-\nprojects/mock-fantasy